% String definitions for \bibliography{strings,refs}; the file is kept so the documented
% order resolves, and it may stay comment-only.
%
% Tectonic's BibTeX implementation drops inter-word spaces when it expands @string macros,
% so a bibliography that relies on them renders as
% "In AdvancesinNeuralInformationProcessingSystems30" under Tectonic, while BibTeX through
% latexmk renders it correctly. Prefer literal field values in refs.bib unless you build
% only with latexmk + BibTeX. When a paper's own bibliography defines @string macros, read
% them for reference and copy the resolved text into literal values here.